{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/897029-help-with-a-character-concept-and-a-question-regarding-lairs","id":897029,"title":"Help with a Character Concept and a Question regarding lairs","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-23T11:49:30-07:00","id":897029,"title":"Help with a Character Concept and a Question regarding lairs","content":"Hi i'm looking for help to pull off a character concept, would love some help.<br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=431\" data-tempid=\"temp_431_1464029340769_562\" /><br /> I'm wanting to build Kindred The Eternal Hunters (Lamb &amp; Wolf) as a Beast. (For those interested in Lore, <a href=\"http://leagueoflegends.wikia.com/wiki/Kindred/Background\" target=\"_blank\">http://leagueoflegends.wikia.com/wik...red/Background</a> )<br /> But i'm struggling on what to do with Wolf. Is there a way to make him as one of two horrors, the other being lamb? Or should I just get True Friend, Retainer and make Wolf a separate Beast entirely.<br /> I am tempted to make them Anakim due to the hopelessness title, since in the lore they are their worlds Grim Reaper and tell everyone that fleeing from them is useless, that undeath won't save them, but I am leaning towards Eshmaki due to them being Hunters. Struggling to make a choice and stick with it.<br /> <br /> And for the Question of Lairs, is their a way to have different enviromental hazards for different chambers? For instance in one Chamber I want it to be a sprawling forest, while the other I want to be the Local Hospital but being overgrown and falling apart. My back up character concepts need to know this too since my non copy right infringing Yogg-Saron character was going to have an abandoned Skyskrapper where Elevator shafts lead to water and eventually the heart of his lair.<br /> <br /> Edit: What I mean with Wolf is, When the beast enters the lair and fuses with their horror, it isn't just Wolf or Lamb there hunting anyone in the lair, its both of them. In order to do that, would I need True Friend + Retainer or is there something in Beast that allows this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2448,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","user":"Dante","date":".  Just Realized an easier way to explain what I mean. 05-23-2016, 05:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T13:55:45-07:00","id":897147,"title":"","content":"You could always make them Anakim Predators. For Lair traits, Undergrowth might be appropriate, since you said that the hospital is overgrown. Maybe Maze?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-23T14:25:27-07:00","id":897185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/897029-help-with-a-character-concept-and-a-question-regarding-lairs?p=897147#post897147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You could always make them Anakim Predators. For Lair traits, Undergrowth might be appropriate, since you said that the hospital is overgrown. Maybe Maze?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I just decided i'll just take Overgrowth and Downpoor, though im still wondering how to make it so Lamb and Wolf are running around the Lair when the beast has merged with its Horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2448-dante","name":"Dante","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2448_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}